## 6. Controller

```java
@GetMapping("/api/numbers/{number}/summary")
public PhoneSummary summary(@PathVariable String number,
                            @RequestParam(required = false) NumberType type) throws IOException {
    return service.getSummary(number, type);
}

@GetMapping("/api/numbers/{number}/expressions")
public ExpressionPage expressions(@PathVariable String number,
                                  @RequestParam(required = false) NumberType type,
                                  @RequestParam(defaultValue = "100") int size,
                                  @RequestParam(required = false) String pitId,
                                  @RequestParam(required = false) List<String> searchAfter) throws IOException {
    return service.getExpressions(number, type, Math.min(size, 1000), pitId, searchAfter);
}
```

Spring converts `?type=MOBILE` to the enum automatically. If the UI already knows the type (e.g. separate "phone" / "mobile" search boxes), always pass it — a single `term` on one field is cheaper than the `bool/should`, and you skip the `byType` resolution entirely.

## Quick notes

- **`exists` vs `numberType` field:** `exists` on a keyword field is fast (it uses doc values / norms), and scoped to ~50k docs it's negligible. But if you ever need to *aggregate across all numbers* by type, index an explicit `numberType` keyword instead.
- **Normalisation:** make sure phone and mobile are stored in the same format (e.g. E.164, no spaces/dashes) or the `term` queries won't match. If they're not, add a `normalizer` on both keyword fields or clean the input in the service before querying.
- **`copy_to` caveat:** `number` is only populated for docs indexed *after* the mapping change — existing 2B docs won't have it without a reindex/update-by-query, so use Option B until then.
